**PART A: the three edits.**
1. **(A-1, B691-1: the row cannot stay green on the lower bound or a wrong figure).** Immediately after the existing `Assert.Throws<Xunit.Sdk.InRangeException>(() => AssertHolds(logged, held));` add ONE assertion with the gate's exact predicate: `Assert.True(logged > held.Ms + Slack, ...)` whose message names the stage and prints `logged`, `held.Ms` and the bound. It must not call `AssertHolds` and must not be computed from the literal 1400. Why: `logged > held.Ms + Slack` is exactly what the upper bound of `Assert.InRange` throws on, so a stage that logged less than its own wait (P3) or a row that read another figure (Q) now fails here, with a message saying so, while the real red case (1400 added) satisfies it with the measured 208-224 ms of margin on SQL Server. `Slack`, `AssertHolds`, the literal and the exception type check stay as they are.
2. **(A-2, B691-3: the stale parenthesis).** On the one line of the `Slack` doc comment that reads `(finer: green at 1190, red at 1200)`, replace exactly that parenthesis with a sentence-faithful reword that says the cut lies at about 1200 ms less the few ms the stage already spends outside its wait, with no claim that 1190 is green and none that it is red (suggested text, yours to improve in ASCII: `(finer: the cut lies at about 1200 less the few ms the stage already spends outside its wait)`). This is the ONE existing line you change; every other character of the comment, including `SQL Server: not measured` and the HPSMPOC-318 paragraph, is byte-equal to the base. Do NOT write that the floor was measured on SQL Server.
3. **(A-3, B691-5: the reset must not depend on run order).** Add to `StagedFactory` ONE `public static` (or `internal static`) read accessor over its three statics (`_armed`, `_only`, `_addedMs`; rest value 0 for each), with a one-line doc comment, and in the row, **right after the try/finally and before the log line is read**, assert that all three are at rest, so a failure names the static that is not (for example one `Assert.Equal` per static, or a tuple compare whose message names them). Rest means: not armed, no stage named, nothing added (exactly what `DisarmOnly` restores). Why there: the row's `finally` and `DisarmOnly` have just run, so a missing reset fails THIS row in any run order, not the staged test at position 20 only when the rows ran first. Record in STATUS that the `finally` itself cannot be pinned without planting a throw (gate mutant L): the pin is on what `DisarmOnly` does, which is the part a later test depends on; that is the ticket's "records why a line cannot be pinned" branch for that one line.
